{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Phase 2 — repair, verification, and disposition\n\nGerrit change **1990** (`d782511ffb` pre-rebase), rebased onto current `origin/main`.\n\n### The fix\nHelper recognition now fails CLOSED, symmetrically with the `os.environ`-attribute seam.\nThe trigger is **dataflow, not spelling**: a function whose `os.environ` key expression\nreferences one of its OWN parameters is an env-read helper by construction, because its\neffective variable names are supplied by its callers. Missing from `KNOWN_ENV_HELPERS` →\n`UnregisteredEnvReadHelper` (a new class, kept distinct from `UnrecognisedEnvironAccess` so\nthe two seams stay separately diagnosable), naming every offending site in one raise.\n\nRows added for the three shims the census found: `_gate_str_pref`, `read_secret_env`,\n`_env_truthy`. `scan()` keeps its 2-tuple arity — the fail-closed signal is the exception,\nnever a third element.\n\n### RED -> GREEN, with the oracle held out\nThe five tests were written and proven RED **before** the fix existed, then moved OUT of the\ntree; the implementing subagent was given only the contract (the postcondition), never the\ntests, and was denied the whole `tests/` directory.\n\n| stage | result |\n|---|---|\n| RED (primary) | `DID NOT RAISE RuntimeError` — the silence itself |\n| RED (real tree) | `['REBAR_GATE_REF', 'REBAR_GATE_SOURCE']` missing |\n| RED (b00f replay) | \"returned silently after losing 4 variable(s)\" — the original four |\n| GREEN | all 5 pass against an implementation that never saw them |\n\n**Mutation check (the tests have teeth).** Re-narrowing recognition to the pre-fix fail-open\nbehaviour returns both mechanism tests to RED with their original messages. Separately,\ndeleting the `_gate_str_pref` row now aborts with\n`UnregisteredEnvReadHelper: - _gate_str_pref defined at src/rebar/_config_resolvers.py:297`\n— the exact scenario that lost the two keys is now a named, actionable failure instead of\nsilence.\n\n**Refactoring litmus.** Every assertion is on observable behaviour — a raised exception, its\nmessage text, and the contents of the returned `reads` mapping. No private names, no source\ngreps, so a behaviour-preserving refactor keeps them green.\n\n### The artifact was regenerated (162 -> 164)\n`docs/env-vars.md` gains `REBAR_GATE_REF` and `REBAR_GATE_SOURCE`, `JIRA_API_TOKEN` gains\n`src/rebar/config.py` as a reader, and the header prose now states both halves are\nfail-closed. A generator fix leaving a stale artifact is half a fix.\n\n### The repo-wide oracle that bit 1979 twice — it fired here too\nRegistering `read_secret_env` made a REAL credential read visible to\n`scripts/check_config_ownership.py`, which imports `KNOWN_ENV_HELPERS`: the `JIRA_API_TOKEN`\npresence probe at `config.py:551`. Proven caused by this change (popping the three new rows\nin-process returns the gate to clean), so it was NOT silenced by dropping the row.\n\nThe read is correctly placed — `bool()` discards the value at the composition root, and\n`read_secret_env`'s own docstring already declares config.py THE owned seam — so it takes the\nnarrow one-line `# read-via: credential-presence` marker, the documented escape already used\nfor credential boundaries elsewhere (`credential-injection`, `cli-credential-boundary`),\nrather than making all of `config.py` a credential boundary or filing it as legacy debt.\nThis is a small net WIN: the ownership gate now sees a credential read it was blind to for\nexactly the reason the registry was blind to `REBAR_GATE_REF`.\n\n### Gates (run here, not delegated to CI)\n`make lint` 0 · `make typecheck` 0 (615 files) · complexity ratchet\n`active=49 new=0 increased=0 stale=0` · **`tests/unit` 11979 passed, 44 skipped** ·\n**`tests/scripts` 1048 passed, 2 skipped** (this is the suite whose ~40 held-out\nownership-gate tests transitively `scan(src/rebar)`) · `gen_env_registry.py --check` 0 ·\n`check_config_ownership.py` 0. All re-verified AFTER the rebase.\n\n### Step 7 sweep — both axes\n**Construct axis.** The class is \"a name-keyed env-read recognition table whose absence is\nsilent\". It exists in exactly two places, and the second (`check_config_ownership.py`)\n*imports* the table rather than reimplementing it, so there is no third instance to drift.\n`scripts/check_config_reads.py` looked like a candidate and is not — it is a schema-field\ngate with no env recogniser.\n\n**Parity axis.** Rule, stated without naming the fixed site: *recognition of an environment\nread must fail closed — a read the generator cannot fully resolve aborts the run naming the\nsite, never gets walked past.* Channel census:\n\n| surface | status |\n|---|---|\n| CLI (`gen_env_registry.py`, `--check`) | holds — goes through `scan()` |\n| MCP / API tool | N/A — the generator has no MCP surface |\n| library consumer (`check_config_ownership.py`) | holds by delegation: `check()` -> `derive_env_baseline()` -> `scan()` |\n| automated callers (CI docs-gates, `make lint`) | holds |\n| dual-direction (the MIRROR operation) | **MISSING** — see below |\n\nThe mirror of \"helper with no row\" is \"row with no helper\". 4 of 11 rows are ghosts with no\n`def` site. Disposition: **ticket filed**, `surprised-convincing-gopher`\n(`84c7-486f-9a13-4c3f`), linked `discovered_from` this ticket. Deliberately not fixed here —\nit causes no key loss today, and folding it in would widen the diff past the proven mechanism.\n\n### Scope & safety\nCaller-dependency sweep: the one behavioural consumer is `check_config_ownership.py`, handled\nabove; arity preserved. The fix RESTORES the registry's completeness contract rather than\ncreating capability. No new dependency. **No test was weakened** — the two test files are\nappend-only, and no pre-existing assertion was removed, loosened, skipped, or xfailed.\n\n### Residual risk\n- **Accepted:** the `# read-via:` marker means the ownership gate no longer flags\n  `config.py`'s presence probe. That is the mechanism's documented purpose and it carries a\n  named rationale; the invariant it asserts (the value never leaves the boundary) is enforced\n  by the `bool()` on the same line.\n- **Ticket filed:** ghost rows, above.\n- Nothing else observed.\n\n### Replication\nThe original report replicates as resolved through the real entry point, not just the unit\ntest: `python scripts/gen_env_registry.py --check` exits 0 against a committed registry that\nnow CONTAINS the two keys, and the seam comment at `_config_resolvers.py:288-289` — \"the\nenv-name literals stay visible to `gen_env_registry` here\" — is true for the first time."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787303868879505001,"uuid":"d1d2fc07-e389-47ca-a841-0559db954eb8"}